00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:01.910 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  one o'clock in central kabul and taliban  security forces run towards the site of  an explosion smoke leads them towards  dalhan military hospital across the road  from the now abandoned u.s embassy  one device was detonated at the hospital  entrance allowing attackers to move in  20 minutes later a second exploded  inside the compound  this man films from inside the hospital  repeating god have mercy on us as he  watches the attack take place  people shelter where they can as fires  from the explosions burn and gunmen move  between buildings  dozens of others managed to reach the  back of the hospital compound  watchtowers and security walls that were  meant to keep them safe in sight now  their biggest obstacle to escape  above afghan air force helicopters  circled flown by pilots from the  previous government who are now part of  the taliban's defence  taliban responded by sending their  special forces to the site of the attack  after the first explosion and they've  created quite a large cordon around  where the attack has taken place as  spread at gunfire has continued  throughout the afternoon  there were two explosions and six  attackers all of them were killed the  security forces of the taliban are in  the area and our special badger units  are here who are very quick in their  operations the whole area is now under  our control  the taliban know how to secure the  military hospital because they know its  weaknesses they attacked it themselves  ten years ago  isil fighters also targeted the hospital  in 2017  then they dressed as doctors to evade  security more than 100 people were  killed and injured  isil has challenged the taliban's  hold-on security since it came to power  in august the group has carried out four  major bombings and killed hundreds of  civilians the worst was at kabul airport  as tens of thousands of people evacuated  the last foreign military forces  withdrew  the main thing that people really much  need and want from taliban was  their grip over the security and their  last era if they lose  that grip  if the  insecurity increases i think  it will somehow  discredit taliban's presence in the  power  the taliban has downplayed the threat of  isil but the group is getting harder to  ignore taliban casualties are mounting  as isil targets its members particularly  in eastern provinces  still in kabul taliban members respond  like the previous government would have  just a few months ago they've set up a  large cordon to protect the public  special forces and air cover are  deployed intelligence units gather  evidence but people here are hoping for  more a stop to attacks altogether  charlotte ballas al jazeera kabul

